sn16.10:4.1 | S: Mahākassapa heard Thullatissā say these words, | T: The Venerable Mahakassapa overheard the bhikkhunī Thullatissa making this statement
sn16.10:4.2 | S: and he said to Ānanda, | T: and said to the Venerable Ānanda:
sn16.10:4.3 | S: “Is that right, Reverend Ānanda? Am I the needle peddler and you the needle maker? | T: “How is it, friend Ānanda, am I the needle-peddler and you the needle-maker,
sn16.10:4.4 | S: Or am I the needle maker and you the needle peddler?” | T: or am I the needle-maker and you the needle-peddler?”
sn16.10:4.5 | S: “Forgive her, sir. The lady’s a fool.” | T: “Be patient, Venerable Kassapa, women are foolish.”
sn16.10:4.6 | S: “Hold on, Reverend Ānanda! Don’t make the Saṅgha investigate you further! | T: “Hold it, friend Ānanda! Don’t give the Saṅgha occasion to investigate you further.
sn16.10:5.1 | S: What do you think, Reverend Ānanda? | T: What do you think, friend Ānanda,
sn16.10:5.2 | S: Was it you who the Buddha brought up before the Saṅgha of mendicants, saying: | T: was it you that the Blessed One brought forward in the presence of the Bhikkhu Saṅgha, saying:
sn16.10:5.3 | S: ‘Mendicants, whenever I want, quite secluded from sensual pleasures, secluded from unskillful qualities, I enter and remain in the first absorption, which has the rapture and bliss born of seclusion, while placing the mind and keeping it connected. | T: ‘Bhikkhus, to whatever extent I wish, secluded from sensual pleasures, secluded from unwholesome states, I enter and dwell in the first jhana, which is accompanied by thought and examination, with rapture and happiness born of seclusion.
sn16.10:5.4 | S: And so does Ānanda’?” | T: Ānanda too, to whatever extent he wishes, secluded from sensual pleasures, secluded from unwholesome states, enters and dwells in the first jhana’?”
