## sn46.4
sn46.4:1.1 | S: At one time Venerable Sāriputta was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. | T: On one occasion the Venerable Sāriputta was dwelling at Savatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anathapiṇḍika’s Park.
sn46.4:1.2 | S: There Sāriputta addressed the mendicants: | T: There the Venerable Sāriputta addressed the bhikkhus thus:
sn46.4:1.3 | S: “Reverends, mendicants!” | T: “Friends, bhikkhus!”
sn46.4:1.4 | S: “Reverend,” they replied. | T: “Friend,” they replied.
sn46.4:1.5 | S: Sāriputta said this: | T: The Venerable Sāriputta said this:
sn46.4:2.1 | S: “There are these seven awakening factors. | T: “Friends, there are these seven factors of enlightenment.
sn46.4:2.2 | S: What seven? | T: What seven?
sn46.4:2.3 | S: The awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion, and equanimity. | T: The enlightenment factor of mindfulness, the enlightenment factor of discrimination of states, the enlightenment factor of energy, the enlightenment factor of rapture, the enlightenment factor of tranquillity, the enlightenment factor of concentration, the enlightenment factor of equanimity.
sn46.4:2.4 | S: These are the seven awakening factors. | T: These are the seven factors of enlightenment.
sn46.4:2.5 | S: In the morning, I meditate on whichever of these seven awakening factors I want. | T: “Whichever of these seven factors of enlightenment I want to dwell in during the morning, I dwell in that factor of enlightenment during the morning.
sn46.4:2.6 | S: At midday, | T: Whichever I want to dwell in during the middle of the day, I dwell in that factor of enlightenment during the middle of the day.
sn46.4:2.7 | S: and in the evening, I meditate on whichever of these seven awakening factors I want. | T: Whichever I want to dwell in during the evening, I dwell in that factor of enlightenment during the evening.
sn46.4:2.8 | S: If it’s the awakening factor of mindfulness, I know that it’s limitless and that it’s properly implemented. While it remains I understand that it remains. | T: “If, friends, it occurs to me, ‘Let it be the enlightenment factor of mindfulness,’ it occurs to me, ‘It’s measureless’; it occurs to me, ‘It’s fully perfected.’ While it persists, I understand, ‘It persists. ’
sn46.4:2.9 | S: And if it subsides in me I understand the specific reason it subsides. … | T: If it abates in me, I understand, ‘It has abated in me for a particular reason.’ …
sn46.4:2.10 | S: If it’s the awakening factor of equanimity, I know that it’s limitless and that it’s properly implemented. While it remains I understand that it remains. | T: “If, friends, it occurs to me, ‘Let it be the enlightenment factor of equanimity,’ it occurs to me, ‘It’s measureless’; it occurs to me, ‘It’s fully perfected.’ While it persists, I understand, ‘It persists.’
sn46.4:2.11 | S: And if it subsides I understand the specific reason it subsides. | T: But if it abates in me, I understand, ‘It has abated in me for a particular reason.’
sn46.4:3.1 | S: Suppose that a ruler or their chief minister had a chest full of garments of different colors. | T: “Suppose, friends, a king or a royal minister had a wardrobe full of differently coloured clothes.
sn46.4:3.2 | S: In the morning, they’d don whatever pair of garments they wanted. | T: Whatever suit he might want to wear in the morning he would wear in the morning.
sn46.4:3.3 | S: At midday, | T: Whatever suit he might want to wear during the middle of the day he would wear during the middle of the day.
sn46.4:3.4 | S: and in the evening, they’d don whatever pair of garments they wanted. | T: Whatever suit he might want to wear in the evening he would wear in the evening.
sn46.4:3.5 | S: In the same way, in the morning, | T: So too, friends, whichever of these seven factors of enlightenment I want to dwell in during the morning …
sn46.4:3.6 | S: at midday, | T: during the middle of the day …
sn46.4:3.7 | S: and in the evening, I meditate on whichever of these seven awakening factors I want. | T: during the evening, I dwell in that factor of enlightenment during the evening.
sn46.4:3.8 | S: If it’s the awakening factor of mindfulness, I know that it’s limitless and that it’s properly implemented. While it remains I understand that it remains. | T: “If, friends, it occurs to me, ‘Let it be the enlightenment factor of mindfulness’ … all as above …
sn46.4:3.9 | S: And if it subsides I understand the specific reason it subsides. … | T: (none)
sn46.4:3.10 | S: If it’s the awakening factor of equanimity, I know that it’s limitless and that it’s properly implemented. While it remains I understand that it remains. | T: (none)
sn46.4:3.11 | S: And if it subsides I understand the specific reason it subsides.” | T: I understand, ‘It has abated in me for a particular reason.’”
sn46.4:3.12 | P: Catutthaṁ. | T: (none)


